Licensing changes relative to upstream Dokploy
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Upstream Dokploy was dual-licensed:
  * Most of the code under the Apache License 2.0.
  * A set of enterprise modules, located in "/proprietary" directories, under
    the separate "Dokploy Source Available License" (DSAL). That license only
    permits development/testing use and forbids production use, publishing,
    distribution, or sale without a commercial agreement.

nomploy does not ship any DSAL-licensed code. The enterprise modules were
removed and replaced with original implementations (licensed under AGPL-3.0 as
part of the project) that either provide a free equivalent or cleanly disable the
paid feature. The affected areas are:

  * License gating            -> no commercial licensing; the instance always
                                 runs as the free tier.
  * Custom RBAC roles         -> only the static roles (owner/admin/member).
  * Per-member resource scope -> all members can access all servers and git
                                 providers.
  * SSO (OIDC / SAML)         -> not shipped; email/password auth is used.
  * Social login (GitHub/Google) -> not shipped.
  * Audit logs                -> not shipped (writes are no-ops, reads empty).
  * White-labeling / branding -> available as a free feature.

The replaced files still live under directories named "proprietary" for now to
minimize churn; their contents are original nomploy code (AGPL-3.0), not
Dokploy's proprietary code. These directories may be renamed in a later change.

